DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 5

GitHub Actions – CI/CD Basics (0–2 Years Experience)

In modern DevOps, CI/CD starts directly from GitHub.
For freshers, GitHub Actions is one of the easiest and most powerful CI/CD tools to learn and explain in interviews.

📌 Tool 5 Focus: GitHub Actions Interview Questions

• What is CI/CD and why is it important?
• What is GitHub Actions?
• How is GitHub Actions different from Jenkins?
• What is a workflow in GitHub Actions?
• Where do you define a workflow file?
• What is YAML and why is it used?
• Explain workflow, job, step, and runner
• What are GitHub-hosted runners?
• Difference between GitHub-hosted and self-hosted runners
• What are events in GitHub Actions?
• Explain push, pull_request, and workflow_dispatch
• What is an action from GitHub Marketplace?
• How do you reuse actions?
• What are GitHub secrets?
• How do you store credentials securely in GitHub Actions?
• Difference between environment variables and secrets
• How do you create a simple CI pipeline?
• How do you fail a pipeline intentionally?
• What happens if one job fails?
• Common mistakes beginners make in GitHub Actions
• Real-world use case of GitHub Actions in DevOps

💡 Interview Tip:
If you can clearly explain:
 “Code push → GitHub Actions CI → Build → Test → Deploy”
you already sound like a production-ready DevOps engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience.
